    "message": "docs: bring the public docs up to 5.48.0, and fix what was already wrong\n\nThe docs were current as of 5.41.1. Eight releases landed since. Refreshing\nthem turned up three things that were wrong before this arc started, which\nwere worth more than the refresh.\n\nARCHITECTURE.md had been describing deleted code as current architecture\nsince 5.44.0. It listed quota probes, command prefix detection and filepath\nextraction by name, with their behaviour, as three of five live optimization\nrules. All three were removed three releases ago after firing zero times in\n153,198 real requests. The contract test written for that deletion pins\nSettings, the admin manifest, the handlers, the detectors and .env.example --\nso a partial revert fails -- and says nothing whatsoever about prose. It\npassed happily the entire time.\n\nThe RTK pinned version was stale in three separate places after one bump,\nstill 0.44.2 in the README feature table, ARCHITECTURE and USAGE.\n\nFALLBACK_SKIP_KINDS had never been documented in any user-facing doc, in any\nrelease. Not stale: absent. Nothing looks for absence.\n\nAlso corrected, on the owner's call: CONTRIBUTING.md told contributors to\nclone Alishahryar1/free-claude-code, and RELEASE-CHECKLIST.md called that the\n\"primary fork / development remote\". Neither matches how the repo is run --\nall development and every release goes to FiredMosquito831/my-claude-code,\nand upstream is never pushed to. A contributor following the old instructions\ncloned a repo containing none of the work and built a package whose name did\nnot match the checkout. Both now describe the real topology, with upstream\nkept for provenance and the `gh --repo` trap called out.\n\nAdded for the arc itself:\n\n- README: a Token Optimizer feature row and section, panel by panel against\n  the real UI labels; a \"Requests Answered Locally\" subsection covering the\n  two new log fields and the \"answered locally · <rule>\" display, which is\n  also a working filter value; the context_length paragraph in failover.\n- USAGE: the Token Optimizer page and its trimming subsection nested under\n  the existing Analytics section, so no anchor was renamed; context_length;\n  RTK gain, pin drift, and an explicit statement that MCC forces RTK's\n  telemetry opt-out and suppresses its consent prompt, so enabling RTK\n  through MCC cannot opt anyone in.\n- ARCHITECTURE: the corrected two-rule list with why the others went; the\n  new failure kind; the tool_result_trimming module and its boundary.\n\nTool-result trimming is documented as off and probably best left off, with\nthe measured numbers rather than a caution: 10.9% more fresh input tokens at\nthe shipped defaults, one near-total cache miss when enabled mid-conversation,\nbreak-even at a ~90.9% baseline hit rate. Numbers were read from the module\ndocstring and .env.example, not retyped from a brief.\n\nEvery default published came from Settings.model_fields. Hardcoded counts were\nchecked rather than assumed: 56 providers, 14 search providers, 66 advanced\noptions and 9 desktop settings all verified correct; only the five-rule count\nand the RTK version were wrong. One suspected-stale claim -- the README's\n\"capped at 50k chars\" -- was checked and is correct, because the 50k to 2M\nraise was a different setting.\n\nVerification\n- 211 tests across the seven doc-parsing guards pass. No guard was weakened\n  or edited; none needed updating, because sections and anchors were added\n  rather than renamed.\n- docs/ANTHROPIC-SUBSCRIPTION.md untouched; its policy guard passes.\n- AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md verified byte-identical to each other.\n- Full suite 4,989 passed / 8 failed, all tests/scripts/test_install_ps1_*.\n\nNo version bump: markdown only, no production path touched.\n\nDeliberately not done\n- docs/CLAUDE-CODE-CONFIG.md documents Claude Code's own env vars, not MCC's.\n  Nothing in these releases touches it; it was not audited for upstream\n  accuracy, which is a different job.\n- No restructuring. A reader who knows the old README still recognises it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
